        "date": "2026-11-08T22:23:05Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): rotary Adaptive sorts the leave-envelope plane as material and refuses a band too narrow for the helix by name\n\nThe known red in rotary_adaptive (radius 6.5 at 19.9 % D against the\n19.7 % law) came from float noise: the wrap's plane 6.500000000000001\nsat one ulp above the leave envelope (6.5), so the bare `>` in\npocket3d_air_split put it in the one-lap air leg. A plane within EPS\nof the envelope is now a material plane (machining3d::entry::air_levels).\nThe bar reads round 2's numbers again: 6.5 at 19.5 % D, and 160,989\nworld moves with 0 in-cut breaks.\n\nWhen the wrap's entry law (machining2d::choose_entry) would narrow the\nasked helix for a developed level, the level is now refused before\nplanning, by name with both radii, and Offset rings cut it. On the 10\nlong window the plan used to narrow the helix to 0.900 and then name a\n15.7 % D overload.\n\nThe r6.2 neck levels (5.7, 5.2) stay refused for out-of-cut travel:\n3.2x and 3.9x unlifted, and the lifted plan reads 48.0 deg over the\n47.5 deg bound. That refusal is decided final for this issue and pinned\nby name. The suite's fixtures move to rotary_adaptive_fixture/ to keep\nthe 400-line law.\n\nFixes #55\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
